      "text": "Reliable case-alert operation needs observable RPC failures and tests that exercise both broken streams and healthy idle periods. The evidence supports capturing diagnostic identifiers, bounded retry checks, demand-aware timeout tests, and synthetic-test monitoring. Independent connector implementations demonstrate local gRPC fixtures and operational counters; live sandbox checks remain a separate layer. Apex event tests do not run external Pub/Sub consumers. The proposed acceptance tests are design recommendations derived from these sources. Community transport experiments illustrate fault categories without establishing universal delivery guarantees.",
